 263:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****               ##### Initialization and Configuration functions #####
 264:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****   ==============================================================================
 265:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****   [..]
 266:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****   This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to initialize the USART
 267:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****   in asynchronous and in synchronous modes.
 268:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****   (+) For the asynchronous mode only these parameters can be configured:
 269:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) Baud Rate
 270:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) Word Length
 271:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) Stop Bit
 272:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) Parity: If the parity is enabled, then the MSB bit of the data written
 273:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****            in the data register is transmitted but is changed by the parity bit.
 274:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****            Depending on the frame length defined by the M bit (8-bits or 9-bits),
 275:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****            please refer to Reference manual for possible USART frame formats.
 276:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) USART polarity
 277:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) USART phase
 278:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) USART LastBit
 279:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****       (++) Receiver/transmitter modes
 280:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c **** 
 281:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****   [..]
 282:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     The HAL_USART_Init() function follows the USART  synchronous configuration
 283:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     procedures (details for the procedures are available in reference manual
 284:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     (RM0430 for STM32F4X3xx MCUs and RM0402 for STM32F412xx MCUs
 285:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****      RM0383 for STM32F411xC/E MCUs and RM0401 for STM32F410xx MCUs
 286:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****      RM0090 for STM32F4X5xx/STM32F4X7xx/STM32F429xx/STM32F439xx MCUs
 287:stm/stm32f4xx/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****      RM0390 for STM32F446xx MCUs and RM0386 for STM32F469xx/STM32F479xx MCUs)).
